+/*
+ * The translation's save (reference/NOTES.md, "The compressed save"). A
+ * slot holds an image: a header (mFRm_en_hdr_t), the save (the same
+ * 0xF980 bytes, header and checksum included) and the letters' extension
+ * (mFRm_en_ext), each compressed with include/af_lz.h, then zeros; or,
+ * when the two do not fit in the slot, the save as the cartridge writes
+ * it. Reads take both, so the cartridge's saves load (without extension).
+ *
+ * Every write is of an image. The normal save and the gyroid's
+ * (func_8008F040_jp) borrow a framebuffer (func_800D97A0_jp: 0x25800
+ * bytes), which holds the image, the save's copy and the compressor's
+ * work; the save menu's write takes them from the game state's heap when
+ * it has room, and writes the cartridge's format when it has not (at a
+ * new game, where play holds the whole heap and nothing has an
+ * extension yet). The boot repair copies a slot's image as it is, and
+ * checks read back the image's pages. Reads decompress from the flash a
+ * page at a time.
